cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Torchio, cite the version you used."
title: "Torchio: a press for static digital scholarly editions"
abstract: >-
  Torchio presses TEI P5 files into static digital scholarly editions:
  multipage sites published from a git repository, with no server and no
  database. Behaviour is assigned to TEI model classes rather than to
  individual element names, so an edition that declares its own elements in
  an ODD inherits their rendering. The engine keeps a register of the
  corrections real editions have demanded of it, with a stated condition of
  falsification.
type: software
